menu "Grohe Dial"

    config GROHE_DEV_FEATURES
        bool "Enable developer-only test features"
        default n
        help
            Compiles in developer-only test hooks that have no place in a
            normal build -- currently just the manual OTA validation hook:
            holding the encoder button for ~5 s while the dial is idle logs
            a request, calls OtaManager::CheckForUpdate() against a
            compile-time test URL, and calls StartUpdate() if an update is
            reported available. See kDeveloperOtaUrl in
            components/app/app.cpp and EncoderInput::IsHeldFor() in
            components/encoder/ for the implementation.

            Disabled by default, and completely compiled out (no code, no
            runtime cost) when disabled. Enable only on a development
            build used to validate components/ota/ on real hardware --
            never for a build meant to actually run day to day, since this
            is a physical-access firmware-update trigger with no
            authentication beyond "someone is holding the button".

endmenu
